            "line_count": 3,
            "preview": "// Indices 1-9 land in bitmap[0] (bits 0-63); indices 65-71 land in bitmap[1] (bits 64-127). // This filter spans both bitmaps of the 72-bit shape. final int[] twoMapValues = { 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 65, 66, 67, 68, 69, 70, 71 };"
          },
          {
            "start_line": 25,
            "end_line": 33,
            "line_count": 9,
            "preview": "// Scenario 1: predicate returns false immediately on the first bitmap call. // processBitMaps must stop and return false after exactly 1 invocation. BloomFilter bf = createFilter(twoMapValues);"
          },
          {
            "start_line": 35,
            "end_line": 46,
            "line_count": 12,
            "preview": "// Scenario 2: predicate accepts bitmap[0] but rejects bitmap[1] (the boundary). // processBitMaps must stop at that boundary and return false. bf = createFilter(twoMapValues);"
          },
          {
            "start_line": 48,
            "end_line": 58,
            "line_count": 11,
            "preview": "// Scenario 3: all set bits (1-4) fit inside bitmap[0] (< 64). // Even though no bits are set in bitmap[1], the shape requires 2 bitmaps, // so processBitMaps must still emit a trailing zero bitmap for bitmap[1]."
